General Splitter ->
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The General splitter is a versatile component used to split messages based on a specified delimiter or criteria
-> It enables the splitting of messages into multiple parts or segments based on the defined role or conditions
-> Splits a composite message into individual messages, but retains the enveloping elements (like the root node)
   in each of the split messages .
-> Each split message contains the original message's structure, including the surrounding tags or elements .
   Useful when the context of the enveloping elements is important for subsequent processing.

The General Splitter splits a composite message comprising N messages into N individual messages,
each containing 1 message with the enveloping elements of the composite message. The term enveloping
elements refers to these elements including the split point. Note elements that follow the one that
is indicated as split point in the original message (but on the same level), are'nt counted as enveloping
elements. They won't be part of the resulting messages.

