                                              Security
 Decryptor->
 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 This is the message transformation step that decrypt a message using a private key that is deployed on
 a tenant. You can use descriptor in scenarios  where you need to secure the communication with a participant
 on the cloud using encryption standards such as PGP or PKCS7#7/cms
 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 PGP Decryptor
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 The PGP (pretty good privacy) Decryptor is used to decrypt or decode data that has been encrypted using
 the PGP encryption standard.
 It enables the decryption of PGP-encrypted messages or files, allowing for the retrieval of the original
 plain text data.

 You use the PGP Decryptor to decrypt a message using OpenPGP standards.
 To decrypt a message, the decryptor step requires a private key that must be deployed on the tenant
 (as part of a PGP Secret Keyring). The PGP Secret Keyring can contain multiple private keys.

 To make sure that the right private key is used for decryption, the encrypted message (processed by the decryptor)
 contains a reference that enables the system to uniquely identify the right key.
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 PKCS#7 Decryptor->
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 The public key cryptography standards #7 decryptor is used to decrypt or decode data that has
 been encrypted using the pkcs#7 encrytion standard
 -> it allows for the decryption of pkcs#7- encrppted messages or files enabling the extraction of the
 original plaintext data.
